2155: The index of the next argument to be processed by the
2156: .B getopts
2157: builtin command (see
2158: .SM
2159: .B "SHELL BUILTIN COMMANDS"
2160: below).
2161: .TP
2162: .B OSTYPE
2163: Automatically set to a string that
2164: describes the operating system on which
2165: .B bash
2166: is executing.
2167: The default is system-dependent.
2168: .TP
2169: .B PIPESTATUS
2170: An array variable (see
2171: .B Arrays
2172: below) containing a list of exit status values from the commands
2173: in the most-recently-executed foreground pipeline, which may
2174: consist of only a simple command
2175: (see
2176: .SM
2177: .B "SHELL GRAMMAR"
2178: above).
2179: \fBBash\fP sets
2180: .SM
2181: .B PIPESTATUS
2182: after executing multi-element pipelines,
2183: timed and negated pipelines,
2184: simple commands,
2185: subshells created with the ( operator,
2186: the
2187: .B [[
2188: and
2189: .B ((
2190: compound commands, and
2191: after error conditions that result in the
2192: shell aborting command execution.
2193: .TP
2194: .B PPID
2195: The process ID of the shell's parent.
2196: This variable is readonly.
2197: .TP
2198: .B PWD
2199: The current working directory as set by the
2200: .B cd
2201: command.
2202: .TP
2203: .B RANDOM
2204: Each time this parameter is referenced, it expands to a random integer
2205: between 0 and 32767.
2206: Assigning a value to
2207: .SM
2208: .B RANDOM
2209: initializes (seeds) the sequence of random numbers.
2210: Seeding the random number generator with the same constant value
2211: produces the same sequence of values.
2212: If
2213: .SM
2214: .B RANDOM
2215: is unset, it loses its special properties, even if it is
2216: subsequently reset.
